nder**"},"114":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-112","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#validation-discipline-used-during-development","content":"docs/&#x2A;*, docs-site/**, shell doc sources, or CI graph"},"115":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-113","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#validation-discipline-used-during-development","content":"Docs gates without a browser, then the export + `//docs:render-check` + the screenshot comparison in the CI container"},"116":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-114","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#validation-discipline-used-during-development","content":"**validate-gate**"},"117":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-115","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#validation-discipline-used-during-development","content":"always"},"118":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-116","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#validation-discipline-used-during-development","content":"Pure bash `scripts/ci_check_only.sh` (no Bazel cold start)"},"119":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-117","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#validation-discipline-used-during-development","content":"**Path filter notes:** `scripts/**` no longer always runs docs — only `//:manage`, `scripts/lib/**`, and `scripts/utilities/**` (shell doc sources). Editing only `.github/workflows/*` runs bazel-core (and gate), not hermetic/docs. Shared setup: `.github/actions/setup-bazel` (pinned Bazelisk + disk/repo + lint-tool caches). See `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `.gitea/workflows/ci.yml`, and `.bazelrc` (`--config=ci`)."},"120":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-118","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#validation-discipline-used-during-development","content":"Use queries heavily:"},"121":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-119","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#ci","content":"See `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (path-filtered jobs + `validate-gate`). **bazel-core** is authoritative for hermetic core tests; docs Playwright runs only in **docs-and-render** (not duplicated in bazel-core)."},"122":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-120","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#ci","content":"Use `--config=ci` on CI runners (higher `--jobs`, `--remote_download_minimal`)."},"123":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-121","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#ci","content":"The classic make-based paths remain for compatibility/legacy."},"124":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-122","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#ci","content":"For Gitea: see gitea-ci-setup.md and `.gitea/workflows/ci.yml` (self-hosted runners + persistent cache volumes recommended)."},"125":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-123","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#ci","content":"Bazel jobs restore disk/repo cache via `.github/actions/setup-bazel` (keyed on `MODULE.bazel.lock` + `.bazelversion`)."},"126":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-124","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#published-lab-images-ghcr","content":"`.github/workflows/publish-images.yml` builds first-party CPU-portable images and publishes them to `ghcr.io/<owner>/<repo>/<id>` on push to `development` / `main`. Pull requests build both architectures (`linux/amd64` + `linux/arm64`) with `type=cacheonly` and do **not** push. Catalog: `.github/container-images.json`."},"127":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-125","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#published-lab-images-ghcr","content":"Image id"},"128":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-126","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#published-lab-images-ghcr","content":"Local tag (unchanged)"},"129":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-127","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#published-lab-images-ghcr","content":"GHCR tags"},"130":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-128","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#published-lab-images-ghcr","content":"`lab-dashboard`"},"131":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-129","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#published-lab-images-ghcr","content":"`lab-dashboard:local`"},"132":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-130","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#published-lab-images-ghcr","content":"`development`, `main`, `sha-<short>`, `latest` (main only)"},"133":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-131","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#published-lab-images-ghcr","content":"`mcp-*` / `context7-proxy` / `doc-ingest`"},"134":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-132","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#published-lab-images-ghcr","content":"`lab-mcp/<name>:local`"},"135":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-133","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#published-lab-images-ghcr","content":"same"},"136":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-134","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#published-lab-images-ghcr","content":"`coder-workspace`"},"137":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-135","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#published-lab-images-ghcr","content":"`spark-lab-coder-workspace:latest`"},"138":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-136","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#published-lab-images-ghcr","content":"same"},"139":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-137","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#published-lab-images-ghcr","content":"Not published here: the contributor `devcontainer` (`.github/workflows/devcontainer-image.yml`), `dashboard/Dockerfile.test`, GPU overlay Dockerfiles (build on Spark), and the Kasm desktop image (`kasm-workspace-image.sh` on the node)."},"140":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-138","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#published-lab-images-ghcr","content":"Cluster manifests stay on `:local` with `imagePullPolicy: IfNotPresent`. After the first successful publish, set the GHCR packages **public** so nodes can pull without `imagePullSecrets`. Rebuild a single image with `workflow_dispatch` (`image=<id>` or `all`)."},"141":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-139","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#security-notes","content":"Never commit real `ansible/inventory/hosts.ini` (it is gitignored)."},"142":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-140","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#security-notes","content":"Kubeconfig, tokens, and SSH material are excluded."},"143":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-141","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#security-notes","content":"The BATS tests mock external commands (including kubectl) so they never touch real clusters or credentials."},"144":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-142","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#security-notes","content":"Bazel runfiles + explicit data dependencies make exactly what is needed visible (no accidental leakage of host files)."},"145":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-143","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#security-notes","content":"`MODULE.bazel.lock` is committed (standard for reproducible Bzlmod) and contains only public registry metadata."},"146":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-144","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#security-notes","content":"See the root `.gitignore` and `.bazelignore` for the full exclusion list."},"147":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-145","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#generated-build-output-stays-out-of-the-workspace","content":"`.gitignore` keeps build output out of commits; only `.bazelignore` keeps it out of the build\ngraph, so the two lists are not interchangeable. Each Next.js app needs its own entry\n(`dashboard/.next/`, `docs-site/.next/`): `next build` copies the app's `BUILD.bazel`,\n`.dockerignore` and `.env.example` into `<app>/.next/standalone/`, and Bazel then loads that\ngenerated tree as a real package. The symptom is `//tests:bazel_file_coverage` failing with\nunsanctioned `glob()` patterns and dangling references under a path nobody wrote.\n`//tests:bats_tooling_test` fails if a directory holding a `next.config.*` ever lacks its\n`.next/` line, and `//tests:bazel_file_coverage_unit` proves the gate honours the list."},"148":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-146","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"The following are modeled with first-class Bazel targets:"},"149":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-147","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"`//:manage` as `sh_binary` (`//:manage`)"},"150":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-148","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Full hermetic BATS suite (vendored bats-core)"},"151":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-149","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Kubernetes manifests and overlays as `filegroup` data"},"152":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-150","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Documentation site (`//docs:serve`, `//docs:docs`, `//docs-site:*`)"},"153":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-151","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Includes `//docs:test_generate_shell_docs`, the docs gates in `//:test-fast`, and the export +\n**real browser screenshots vs goldens** in the docs job (visual diffs fail the job and require\nexplicit approval via `//docs-site:visual-linux -- --update` + PR review)."},"154":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-152","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Ansible validation + convenient playbook launchers (`//ansible:*`)"},"155":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-153","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Dashboard dev / build / test wrappers (`//dashboard:*`)"},"156":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-154","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Contributor environment check (`//:doctor`)"},"157":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-155","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Comprehensive root aliases and test suites"},"158":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-156","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Repo-wide ownership gate: `//tests:bazel_file_coverage` proves every tracked file is named by a\nBazel rule, and that each wildcard `glob()` carries a written reason in `SANCTIONED_GLOBS`.\n`bazelisk build //:everything` is the artifact that gate protects; `//:verify` is the gate set."},"159":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-157","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#current-bazel-coverage","content":"Runtime operations against real hardware (full Ansible playbooks with real inventories, heavy cluster workloads) intentionally remain outside pure Bazel \"build\" semantics and are launched through the `sh_binary` wrappers (`//:manage`, `//ansible:*`)."},"160":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-158","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#using-bazel-for-daily-work","content":"Bazel is the established entry point for every build, test, lint, docs, and operations command. The\nMakefile stays as a compatibility shim for people and jobs without `bazelisk`, and it delegates to\nBazel whenever `bazelisk` is on `PATH`. The few places that still call a script directly (the\ndevcontainer's `postStartCommand` bootstrap, the CI dependency warm-up, `scripts/ci_check_only.sh`)\nare listed with their reasons in project-conventions.md."},"161":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-159","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#development-container","content":"First-class multi-arch contributor environment (`.devcontainer/`): **linux/amd64 + linux/arm64**."},"162":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-160","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#development-container","content":"Host"},"163":{"id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL-161","page_id":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL","tags":["bazel","testing","documentation","devcontainer"],"type":"text","url":"/BUILDING_WITH_BAZEL#development-container",