offLimit`, and NCCL. Overlays **select** and optionally **patch**. Prod has no patches on purpose: production numbers stay auditable in `kimi-job.yaml`."},"4281":{"id":"/operate/overlays-80","page_id":"/operate/overlays","tags":["kustomize","overlays","kubernetes","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/overlays#theory","content":"`manage.sh start-test` applies the test/kimi-test path. `start-kimi` applies production kimi. `start-stack-rounded` applies the rounded overlay. Exclusive Mode B/C are **workload directories** (`glm-5.3-flash`, `deepseek-v4.1-flash`), not the rounded overlay - same for the DSpark, EXL3 TensorFold, and Qwen TensorFold lanes. Each `litellm-*` overlay points the router at one backend profile under `k8s/workloads/litellm/files/profiles/`."},"4282":{"id":"/operate/overlays-81","page_id":"/operate/overlays","tags":["kustomize","overlays","kubernetes","safety"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/overlays#theory","content":"Rounded overlay (Mode A) is mutually exclusive with GLM-5.3-Flash and DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash starts,\nand with the DeepSeek-V4-Flash DSpark, GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 TensorFold, Qwen3.8-27B EXL3,\nQwen3.8-27B TensorFold, and Qwen3.8-Flash-Next TensorFold lanes. Those lanes also refuse each\nother. The CLI refuses collisions."},"4283":{"id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot","page_id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot","type":"page","content":"Patch and reboot","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Operate"],"tags":["reboot","safety","operate","kubernetes"],"url":"/operate/patch-and-reboot"},"4284":{"id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot-0","page_id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot","tags":["reboot","safety","operate","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/patch-and-reboot","content":"OS patch, GPU Operator, drain, stop inference first, and reboot order for DGX Spark nodes."},"4285":{"id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot-1","page_id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot","type":"heading","tags":["reboot","safety","operate","kubernetes"],"url":"/operate/patch-and-reboot#patch-and-reboot","content":"Patch and reboot"},"4286":{"id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot-2","page_id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot","type":"heading","tags":["reboot","safety","operate","kubernetes"],"url":"/operate/patch-and-reboot#sequence","content":"Sequence"},"4287":{"id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot-3","page_id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot","type":"heading","tags":["reboot","safety","operate","kubernetes"],"url":"/operate/patch-and-reboot#after-reboot","content":"After reboot"},"4288":{"id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot-4","page_id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot","tags":["reboot","safety","operate","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/patch-and-reboot#patch-and-reboot","content":"Stop inference before any host reboot"},"4289":{"id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot-5","page_id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot","tags":["reboot","safety","operate","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/patch-and-reboot#patch-and-reboot","content":"Drain vs `manage.sh stop`"},"4290":{"id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot-6","page_id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot","tags":["reboot","safety","operate","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/patch-and-reboot#patch-and-reboot","content":"GPU Operator / driver updates"},"4291":{"id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot-7","page_id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot","tags":["reboot","safety","operate","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/patch-and-reboot#patch-and-reboot","content":"Node order and post-reboot verify"},"4292":{"id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot-8","page_id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot","tags":["reboot","safety","operate","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/patch-and-reboot#patch-and-reboot","content":"Patching Ubuntu or the GPU Operator without pinning unified memory on the way down"},"4293":{"id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot-9","page_id":"/operate/patch-and-reboot","tags":["reboot","safety","operate","kubernetes"],"type":"text","url":"/operate/patch-and-reboot#patch-and-reboot","content":"Coming back with an empty `ai-inference` namespace (by design)"},"4294":{"id":"