 `nvidia-smi -lgc`. Range lock (default 300–2200 MHz)\ncaps peak clocks to avoid sustained 78–88°C temps and thermal shutdowns during\nlong-running inference, with near-zero impact on memory-bound MoE workloads."},"6387":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1229","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"**Idempotency** (core of the utility pattern):"},"6388":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1230","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"`status` reports configured lock range, telemetry, and health classification."},"6389":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1231","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"`run` is a no-op when the configured lock range already matches targets."},"6390":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1232","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"Service install is idempotent (only rewrites unit if content differs)."},"6391":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1233","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"**Lock readback**: NVML only offers setters for locked GPU clocks\n(`nvmlDeviceSetGpuLockedClocks`), so `nvidia-smi` cannot confirm a `-lgc` request.\nLive `clocks.min/max.graphics` are used whenever the driver reports them; otherwise\nthe range applied during the current boot is read from `SPARK_CLOCK_STATE_FILE`\n(default `/var/lib/spark-clock/lock`). `status` names which source it used."},"6392":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1234","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"**Safety**:"},"6393":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1235","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"Never touches ai-inference namespace workloads."},"6394":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1236","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"Requires nvidia-smi; mutation verbs require root (or passwordless sudo)."},"6395":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1237","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"Respects the lab's GPU Operator + nvidia-persistenced."},"6396":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1238","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"Detects PD-degraded states (513–650 MHz / \\~15W) and advises power-cycle."},"6397":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1239","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"`throttle-history` only reads telemetry and appends to its own sample log; it\nissues no nvidia-smi setter and needs no root."},"6398":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1240","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"Usage (CLI):"},"6399":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1241","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"Env overrides: CLOCK\\_FLOOR\\_MHZ, CLOCK\\_CEILING\\_MHZ (TARGET\\_CLOCK\\_MHZ aliases ceiling),\nTHERMAL\\_WARN\\_C, THERMAL\\_HOT\\_C, PD\\_\\* thresholds, THROTTLE\\_WINDOW\\_S,\nTHROTTLE\\_OBSERVE\\_SAMPLES, THROTTLE\\_OBSERVE\\_INTERVAL\\_S, THROTTLE\\_HISTORY\\_RETENTION\\_S,\nTHROTTLE\\_HISTORY\\_MAX\\_SAMPLES."},"6400":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1242","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"Dashboard integration: The UI will call status --json and run/reset subcommands."},"6401":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1243","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#spark-clock","content":"**Recent throttling** (`throttle-history`): the driver keeps cumulative\nmicroseconds per throttle reason (`clocks_event_reasons_counters.*`, driver\n575+), which proves throttling happened but never says when. Each reading\nappends a sample to `SPARK_CLOCK_THROTTLE_HISTORY_FILE` and compares against\nthe previous one, so growth between two samples dates the episode. Verdicts:\n`active` (mask says the GPU is held down now), `recent` (episode inside the\nwindow), `since_boot` (counters grew before the log could cover it), `none`,\nor `unreadable` (pre-575 driver without the counters family). Run it on a\ntimer to keep the lookback honest; exit codes 0/1/2/3/4 name the verdict."},"6402":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1244","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#command-throttle-history","content":"Report whether the GPU thermal-throttled recently, and date the last episode.\nEvery reading appends one sample to the history log, so repeated runs (cron or\na systemd timer) turn cumulative driver counters into dated throttle episodes.\nExit codes: 0 none, 1 throttling in the window, 2 undated since-boot evidence,\n3 driver cannot report counters, 4 usage error."},"6403":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1245","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#sync-hermes-seed--copy-hermes-workspace-dev-profile-into-coder-template-seed","content":"Keeps `hermes/profiles/workspace-dev/` as the single source of truth and\nmirrors tracked files into `k8s/dev/templates/coder-spark-lab/hermes-seed/`."},"6404":{"id":"/generated/shell/reference-1246","page_id":"/generated/shell/reference","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/generated/shell/reference#comma