es). Both lanes must be declared in the\n`switch.port_map` — the topology validator rejects a lone lane."],[4812,"**5-node lab:** three Sparks take three full ports; the fourth port uses a **breakout cable**\n(QSFP-DD to 2× QSFP) and carries two Sparks on lanes `sfpplus4a` and `sfpplus4b` at 200G each.\nBoth lanes must be declared together — the validator rejects a lone breakout lane."],[4805,"**5**"],[4842,"**5**"],[3499,"**90Gi**"],[2265,"**A gate that inspected nothing must fail.** Find-nothing is an error, not a pass. `//lints:mypy` and `//lints:yaml_format` both passed for a long time having examined zero files."],[3258,"**A new data shape.** Put it where its consumers can both see it: `dashboard/lib/types/index.ts` when TypeScript on both sides of a boundary needs it, `scripts/lib/py/lab_types.py` when Python does. If a set is closed, declare it once as an `as const` array (TypeScript) or a `StrEnum` (Python) and derive the rest."],[3259,"**A new gate.** When a convention is easy to violate, encode it as a check rather than relying on reminder. One rule governs new gates, and it is the lesson of this repository's history: a gate that inspected nothing must not pass. `//lints:mypy` used to print `mypy: no tracked Python files` and `exit 0` because `git ls-files` fails in the Bazel runfiles sandbox, so the Python type gate had never once run; `//lints:yaml_format` resolved its repo root one directory too shallow, globbed zero files, and exited `0`. Both now treat an empty file list as a hard failure. If you add a check that can find nothing to check, make finding nothing an error."],[5055,"**Agents**"],[2647,"**All code fences must specify a language** (`bash`, `yaml`, `text`, `mermaid`, etc.)"],[2585,"**Allow-lists:** `ALLOWED_UTILITIES` Set + `UtilityNameSchema`"],[927,"**Ansible**"],[4816,"**Any** of the Sparks can run the K3s server. The declarative topology marks exactly one\nnode with `role: orchestrator`, and the generated inventory derives the groups fro